// ---- Scary sounds: a dread layer under the scene, separate from the music. A low hum bed, then every so often a hit:
// slow booms deep inside, something skittering through the walls past you, a long metal groan. They are made on the
// fly (Web Audio), or come from your own files. Each hit is told to the characters, so they react to it out loud.
// It runs in places marked scary, or while the story's music is scary. Off with the switch on the ready screen.
// Anything that happens in the scene (a sound, a light, a door, a story beat) can be told to the characters, so they
// react for real. It goes in as a short note from the world and the one you're with answers in character. Spaced out
// (one every 25 s at most) and never on top of a reply or while you are talking.
let worldTalkAt=0;
